Z||000027||Fformula88||12-01-2000||10:15 PM||||Now Joe4x4's trucks have that snow-beating ground clearance I am talkin about  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Plus, if your stuck in a trafic jam, you can just drive over it!  LOL  Very nice!<P>Of course, the UniMOG is also a very tempting choice!  Will the Fiero fit in the back?!?!  If so, it would be the perfect transporter!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>But Hugh!  That beauty certainly does not deserve to be driven in bad weather!  Please excuse me, but I don't know older cars too well, as far as recognizing them.  Is it a Chevelle?  It sure is sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000028||hugh||12-01-2000||10:28 PM||||I never ran it on the strip,I built it just for the challenge,took over 5 years and over$20,000.Plus a ton of hours just working out things like the rear suspension,brakes,etc.I don't use it on the street anymore.It's a 1970 Chevelle.||||reg||1
Z||000029||VelociFero||12-02-2000||09:16 PM||||Anybody mention the Celica All-Trac?<BR>These Bad Boys have the MR2 Turbo's engine (3sgte) coupled to an all wheel drive system.||||reg||1
Z||000030||vietnow||12-04-2000||03:50 AM||||hey the 3SGTE isnt the 'mr2s turbo engine'<P>hehe its just the turbo version of the 3SGE that comes on GT and GTS 86-89 celicas..<P>i dunno if the mr2 had it first or what...but i know the 3 series is the celica's engine.<P>but on the topic of the all-trac, you get all wheel drive, sporty ride, and 180 hp!<P>------------------<BR>Vietnow --<BR>1986 Celica GTS||||reg||1
Z||000031||Songman||12-04-2000||03:21 PM||||My old Power Wagon has pulled every other 4x4 around here out of the mud! Of course, with the suspension lifted and sitting on those big ole 35s it will beat you to death to drive it and it gets just under 10mpg with a top speed of around 65!<P>My producer has a 2000 custom built 4x4 Lincoln Navigator! That is my idea of 4x4 in style!||||reg||1
Z||000032||Fformula88||12-04-2000||05:07 PM||||Following on the Celica theme, I would love a Mitsu 3000GT VR-4.  Now thats my idea of four wheel drive!  Only problem is it doesn't exactly have the ground clearance I would be looking for in snow.  ||||reg||1
Z||000033||vietnow||12-04-2000||08:23 PM||||<BR>yeah the VR-4 is like a celica all-trac and a supra TT's baby.<P>but the VR-4's are plagued with problems in the AWD system.<P>On top of that, they are semi-rare, and expensive as hell.<P><P>------------------<BR>Vietnow --<BR>1986 Celica GTS||||reg||1
Z||000034||Fformula88||12-04-2000||11:54 PM||||Yeah, they are kinda rare, but there is a big Mitsu dealer a few miles from my house that seems to have one nearly all the time on his lot... usually around 20K asking price.  A little steep for me considering they have tons of miles on them and never are in very good shape.<P>There is also the Mitsu Eclipse AWD Turbo.<P>Or better yet, the new Audi TT with the Quatro awd tranny! I think they look sweet, and they aren't priced too bad for the amount of car you get!<P>Or while I am dreaming, the Porshe Carrera 4!! hehehe   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
